From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: stop PPE peer routing on bridge join

A VAP can be attached to a Linux bridge after its PPE direct-switch VP was
created.  In that case an already authorized peer could keep the RxOLE
peer-routing bit set even though the VAP has entered a software L2 flood
domain.  Clear the firmware route and host search entry before returning
to the bridge path; teardown still clears the peer mapping through the
normal disable operation.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -1430,4 +1431,21 @@ void ath12k_ppe_ds_peer_route(struct ath
+	struct wireless_dev *wdev = ieee80211_vif_to_wdev(vif);
+
 	if (!ppe->started || arvif->ppe_vp < 64)
 		return;
 
+	/* A VAP may join its software bridge after the PPE VP was
+	 * allocated.  Do not leave an authorized peer on the direct
+	 * RxOLE path, which cannot flood the bridge's L2 broadcasts.
+	 */
+	if (enable && wdev && wdev->netdev &&
+	    netif_is_bridge_port(wdev->netdev)) {
+		ath12k_wmi_config_peer_ppeds_routing(ar, arsta->addr,
+						     arvif->vdev_id,
+						     arvif->ppe_vp, false);
+		if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)
+			ath12k_hif_write32(ab, ATH12K_PPE_SEARCH_TABLE_BASE +
+				   arvif->ppe_search_idx * 4, 0);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION && track_peer) {
